{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the page's no-session words at head 66d3dc84, for request 278db3de and review request 54682eeb. Verdict: APPROVED. Only words change, the refusal stays under 61cc5e50, and the words tell a person a cause and a next step that the old sentence did not. Two sentences can improve at the next edit, and neither blocks. This changes the page bundle, and the planner deploys it.\n\n## Your five questions\n\n1. **The sentences against what each reason can say: all hold except one verb.**\n   - `sessions-unavailable` is exact. `sessions.ts:372` answers it when the service has no sessions or no request store, before it reads the request. \"Is not giving read sessions to any key\" and \"did not check\" both follow.\n   - `rate-limited`, `clock-behind` and `expired` with \"may be wrong\" say no more than their reasons.\n   - `no-reply` says \"did not answer\". That is false for a late or malformed reply. See question 3.\n   - \"Signed there recently\" simplifies the window, and the note says so.\n2. **`unauthorized` for a person whose key was revoked as compromised: the right next step.** Someone in the room must act, and the invitation form takes both `artroom-invite:` and device links, so a new link gets that person a new key. The sentence does not say \"your key was stolen\", and it cannot, because the page cannot tell that from the other cases. Someone holding the stolen key reads the same words. They gain nothing they did not have, because anyone can ask for a link, and the person they ask decides.\n3. **Can a reply steer the words: only within a closed set.** `isSessionAnswer` closes the reasons against `REFUSALS`, so the `default` case can print only a known word such as `replayed`. A 429 must also carry `rate-limited`. The service can still state a false reason, but it also serves this page, so the page has no stronger source to compare it with. The one inexact case is yours: `no-reply` covers a late or malformed reply. At the next edit, write \"did not give a usable answer\". Reload is still the right step.\n4. **The Details line: nothing a stranger should not read.** It holds the directory's scope ID, which the saved room already holds, and a word about that key's own session request.\n5. **A later refused read on an open room: not in this head.** The request names the open, and a mid-page failure needs its own words, because the person may have unsent work there. The note lists it.\n\n## One case I did not settle\n\n`initializationMessage` shows the words whenever the rules state is `unknown` and the room holds no session. `noSessionWords` was written for a key that failed to open. A founder whose first session request fails during the room's first moments could read \"Ask someone in the room for a new invitation link\" in the room they just made. A room opened with no session also stays on signed reads until a reload, so the notice would stay too. I did not trace whether that timing can happen, and neither your cases nor the witness show it. If it can, a reload clears it, and nothing is signed or lost. So I do not block on it. Check it at the next edit of this text, or list it in the note's open limits.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. `Unreadable` carries the reason, and only a `forbidden` directory read on open sets it. `shell.ts` holds the words, so the screen and the forms cannot drift apart.\n\n**Security.** No issue. The page learned nothing new about any key: a stranger could already tell from the session route's own status. The refusal under 61cc5e50 does not change.\n\n**Simplification.** Good. One table of words replaces a raw error. `noSessionOf` reads the field by shape instead of by class, which is what lets `shell.ts` stay free of `data.ts`.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The source diff, the note, `requestSession` as far as its reply checks, and the refusal at `sessions.ts:372`. I read the names of the new tests, not their bodies. I did not read `no-session-screens.mjs` or view the screenshots.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `3d6f4639…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `162edc1a`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3467 plain and 935 native tests. The diff from there to this head touches only the note and its manifest. The unit holds the 9 control logs and each names a failed assertion. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `no-session-words.scope.test.ts` and `story.scope.test.ts` pass 6 of 6. `settings.test.ts` and `view.test.ts` pass 16 of 16. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 10 with 0 failures. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, and `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged. The worktree stayed clean. The head includes main 8ae17cb2.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader. No deployed Worker has run this code, and nothing has run a real 429.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bef24dfe3c2e615802c9ef5ac166ddd78341388d","binding":"assigned","head":"66d3dc84e60e83560ecca4c096129a92715d959f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a6ca09b5d99aaf7850d48787127d1b6615a27c1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5919cf68897a494e1eb89819042a3011e0272e4d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a6ca09b5d99aaf7850d48787127d1b6615a27c1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}